Chapter: State

 The State effect declares two operations for reading and writing a single mutable cell of type s.

 To get-state gives s under the State effect, returning the current value.
 To set-state gives Nothing under the State effect, replacing the current value.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  effect State where
    get-state : [State] s
    set-state : s -> [State] Nothing

